While nitrogen properly namespaced all struct definitions, nested usages, and even imports, there was one case where namespacing didn't work properly; when generating the `JSIConverter<T>` extension for the custom type `T`.

Previously nitrogen generated this code:

```cpp
namespace margelo::nitro {
  using namespace margelo::nitro::image;
  struct JSIConverter<ResizeMode> { ... }
}
```

..which was problematic, because the `using namespace …` directive will alias all types from that namespace - if a second namespace (e.g. `margelo::nitro::video`) also contains `ResizeMode`, those two symbols will conflict.

To fix this, nitrogen now generates fully qualified namespaced `JSIConverter<T>` extensions like so:

```cpp
namespace margelo::nitro {
  struct JSIConverter<margelo::nitro::image::ResizeMode> { ... }
}
```

And, as you can see, this even works for nested properties: https://github.com/mrousavy/nitro/blob/7f66356f230bcec46842ecaafc91cc0e3b36215e/packages/react-native-nitro-test/nitrogen/generated/shared/c%2B%2B/Car.hpp#L65-L66

